/*
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: no
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
 *
 * Stylesheet of the Companion OS installer branding. Colours are CTRL_* placeholders between at-signs that stage-installer.sh fills with the
 * brand tokens (vendor/brand/tokens/tokens.sh, see the table in that script): the brand canon is the only place a hex value is typed
 * (the style-canon lint reads this tree).
 *
 * Why there is more than a font size here. The installer takes its colours from the Plasma colour scheme of the live session,
 * CI-OS-Dark, and that scheme (backends/_mixins/kde-plasma/CI-OS-Dark.colors) paints Window, View, Button AND Selection with the same
 * brand teal (10,99,88). Everything Qt draws with the palette's Highlight is therefore invisible, which is what the ISO #4 frames showed:
 *   - the progress bar of the installing page: its filled part had the window colour, only the unfilled track was lighter (inverted);
 *   - the selected row of the keyboard layout / variant lists, the bootloader list, the package tree and the partition table;
 *   - the Welcome page's help icon, a stock dark pictogram from Calamares' own resources (:/data/images/help.svg), unreadable on teal.
 * The scheme is shared with the Ubuntu edition and not ours to change, so the installer sets its own colours here, for the widgets it
 * actually uses. Verified against the pinned installer (3.4.2-13, the package the launcher keeps): the object names #supportButton,
 * #donateButton, #releaseNotesButton and #knownIssuesButton are the ones its own stock stylesheet uses and are in the strings of its
 * welcome module; the rest are Qt classes (QProgressBar, QAbstractItemView), which Calamares documents as styleable. The result was
 * rendered offscreen with the Breeze style, the CI-OS-Dark palette and this sheet; the installer tests of this edition (installer-config.py)
 * hold the contrast numbers.
 *
 * Contrast (WCAG 2.1, checked by iso/tests/installer-config.py from the resolved tokens, not by eye):
 *   selected row     dark text on sage          13.98:1 (AAA), the row against the window 5.43:1 (needs 3:1 as a graphic)
 *   progress text    light text on the fill      4.58:1 (AA, needs 4.5), on the track 16.16:1
 *   progress fill    against the track           3.53:1 (needs 3:1), the track's outline against the window 3.52:1
 */

QWidget {
    font: 13px;
}

QDialogButtonBox {
    dialogbuttonbox-buttons-have-icons: 0;
}

/*** Installing page: the progress bar.
 *
 * A dark track with a light outline and a brand-teal fill, the percentage centred in it. The text is light on both (the fill is the
 * brightest brand teal on which light text still reads: 4.58:1); a light fill would need dark text, which would not read on the track.
 */
QProgressBar {
    background-color: @CTRL_TRACK@;
    border: 1px solid @CTRL_TRACK_OUTLINE@;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: @CTRL_FILL_TEXT@;
    text-align: center;
    min-height: 18px;
    max-height: 18px;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background-color: @CTRL_FILL@;
    border-radius: 3px;
}

/*** Selected rows of every list, tree and table (keyboard page, bootloader chooser, package groups, partitions, combo box popups).
 *
 * selection-background-color / selection-color set the palette's Highlight / HighlightedText for the view, which is what Breeze paints
 * selected and hovered rows with. The sidebar of the main window has its own delegate and its own colours (branding.desc style:), so
 * it is not touched.
 */
QAbstractItemView {
    selection-background-color: @CTRL_SELECTION@;
    selection-color: @CTRL_SELECTION_TEXT@;
}

/*** Welcome page: the four link buttons.
 *
 * Calamares puts a stock pictogram (dark on transparent) on each of them; on the teal window it is a dark smudge next to the text. The
 * links keep their label and lose the icon. qproperty-iconSize as well as icon-size, because the first sets the widget's own property
 * and wins even if the code of a later Calamares sets an icon size itself.
 */
#supportButton,
#donateButton,
#releaseNotesButton,
#knownIssuesButton {
    icon-size: 0px;
    qproperty-iconSize: 0px 0px;
}
